    "notes": "The hillside museum has a buried triangular spine, narrow glazed ridge, railed entrance bridge, stepped exit, west overlook and integrated Hall of Names roof light. The central ridge and access grades follow the coarse standard terrain. The count of west stairs, exact roof grades, local retaining landscape and rail dimensions are reconstructed from photographs. The integrated Hall of Names roof position and rim profile are approximate. Underground rooms, exhibitions and the visitor route inside the museum remain outside the exterior scope."
  },
